    {
      "ordinal": 8,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "3.3",
      "title": "Eye Slots",
      "body": "● Eye slots should resemble sources for the visor.\n● Eye slots should not exceed 25mm tall to prevent any injury..\\\n● Great helms with two (2) eye slots are permitted to add up to two (2) externally riveted eye bars or buhurt-optimized internal eye bars per eye slot.\n● Great helms with a single eye slot are allowed to add up to five (5) buhurt-optimization eyebars: one (1) in the middle and two (2) on each side.\n● It is not possible to mix externally riveted eyebars and buhurt-optimization eyebars on the same helmet. Only one type of eyebar is allowed.\n● Eyebars must conform to the Eyebars Rules document.",
      "page_from": 5,
      "page_to": 5,
      "stable_key": "great-helms:3.3",
      "parent_key": "great-helms:3",
